We propose a novel regularized conditional Wasserstein GAN, which enables the generation of posterior samples under a given label in imaging applications. By reinterpreting the CWGAN objective in a way that is amenable to regularization, we derive a theoretical framework indicating that with smooth and bijective constraints, our model produces realistic samples from the posterior distribution defined by a given label. To validate the effectiveness of our R-CWGAN, we conducted synthetic data and real-world MRI reconstruction experiments, demonstrating superior performance compared to traditional WGAN implementations. 

